cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ilang-conformance, please cite it as below."
title: "ilang-conformance: a deterministic conformance test set for the iLang protocol"
abstract: >-
  ilang-conformance tests whether a language model reachable over an API
  follows the iLang protocol when the specification is in its context. Every
  model answers the same 320 cases in three tracks (grammar 120, exec 100,
  judge 100), and deterministic code scores each answer with the upstream
  validators vendored at a pinned commit of the iLang canon. No model grades
  another model, and no score is assigned by hand. Version 1.0.0 publishes the
  first result set: 45 scored model runs made between 18 and 20 September 2026,
  34 of them complete and comparable, with weighted totals from 0.0278 to
  0.8417 and no run at the L1 gate. The execution track separates the field,
  and of 2,558 rule violations counted there, 2,387 fall on the single rule
  that forbids a model from signing a state declaration with an authority it
  does not hold. The runs were made through two aggregator relays rather than
  the vendors' own APIs; model identity is what the relay returned, and the
  scoreboard records per run what the relay changed or lost. Every published
  score is reproducible from its run records with the scorer in this
  repository.
type: software
